-## Global constraints
-
-- The GDD wins over every older spec (AGENTS.md). Anything the GDD marks Open, Proposal or TBD is built only as the owner's answer. **No PR in this plan decides an open D-row.** Where this plan states a recommendation, it is a recommendation; the owner decides.
-- **Owner questions needed by this phase are decided:** Q-CAMP-2's camp sites; Q-SWAMP-3's Hula sensitivity clearance; and the sensitivity sign-off for Kiryat Shmona and Beit Shemesh.
-- Balance values are labelled design values in `content/` (Q-CUT-1), never invented. Each is the owner's number, or a design value an agent proposed that the owner may override ("Agents propose design values", 15 October 2026, [#375](https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/issues/375#issuecomment-6183538544); Q-COR-6, Q-FIELD-3, Q-SWAMP-1 and Q-VET-1 have one in PR 0's table), with a comment saying it is a design value and which question set it. Sourced facts go in `content/` with `sources:` and a `checked:` date (CONTENT_POLICY §2.1). Dates show as "15 May 1948".
-- **Every site, corridor and waypoint is sourced** (impact plan §4.4: "site names, founding dates and positions; corridor routes"). A route that did not exist on the 1946 map is traced between sourced waypoints and marked `status: draft` with a `to_verify` line, as the Burma Road entry already is. No alignment is invented. Where no source gives one, the PR says so and stops.
-- Determinism (docs/determinism.md): one RNG, no trigonometry, no unordered iteration into state, invariant culture. **No PR in this phase adds an RNG draw.** Progress, Food yield and service are integers. Sites and corridors iterate in ordinal id order, and segments in index order.
-- **Goldens.** After cutover every PR here that changes an MVP rule or the site and corridor data moves the goldens: `hash1950`, `hash1952`, `mvp-end`, `scenario-cautious`, `scenario-reckless`, `scenario-mvp-absorb-first`, `smoke5` if the first five turns change, and `mvp-slice` if Phase 2 kept it. Each re-pins in its own PR, with a rebaseline-history row in docs/determinism.md and the reason in the commit and the PR.
-- **The population anchors hold** (`CalibrationTests`, 3%). No Phase 4 rule moves people between the national head count and the cities.
-- Every new rule gets an `R-` ID in `docs/rules/mvp.md`, defined in the code PR together with its citing test (`rule_ids.py`). The IDs below are **proposed**. R-SITE continues from #566's R-SITE-003. The new area names (R-COR, R-CAMP, R-FIELD, R-SWAMP, R-VET) need the maintainer's sign-off. R-OBJ continues after Phase 3's R-OBJ-004; if Phase 5 takes R-OBJ-005 first, take the next free number. Rewording a rule keeps its ID, and a retired ID is not reused.
-- Each feature gets a `docs/gdd/<feature>.md` section that passes `gdd_lint.py`. **docs/gdd/corridors.md exists (#534):** PR 2 updates it rather than adding a second one. The sites, fields and swamp, and veteran sections are new: `docs/gdd/sites.md` (unless #566 adds one), `docs/gdd/fields-and-swamps.md` and `docs/gdd/veteran-pioneer.md`.
-- **Sensitivity** (CONTENT_POLICY §2 and §4; impact plan §4.1 item 4). No mechanic may turn a depopulated place into housing, jobs, Food or score. A site is designated only if it meets #378's Task 5.0 criterion 4 (it is not on the site of a depopulated Arab locality, unless the owner has seen that stated factually). Corridor segments are named on screen by the corridor's name and a number, not by the villages a source uses as waypoints; those names stay in the map data. Any text that names such a place goes through D-F1 review (Q-SENS-1).
-- Each PR: a branch from current `origin/main` in `.worktrees/<branch>`; a claimed issue (Task form); a `CHANGELOG.md` line for `sim/`, `content/` or `unity/`; commits end with the session's `Co-Authored-By` line; the PR body ends with the session's attribution line; "Refs #384" (never "Fixes" until the last PR of the phase).
-- Full checks before every PR (exact commands in the Phase 1 plan, Global constraints): `dotnet test sim/Statecraft.sln` (0 warnings), the tools and policy pytest runs, `check_repo.py`, `changelog_check.py --base origin/main`, `gdd_lint.py`, `rule_ids.py`, `md_links.py`.
-- Unity: when `unity/` changes or the DLL's behaviour changes, run `tools/build_sim_for_unity.sh`, then EditMode under `machine_lock.py` (the Phase 1 plan's command). Never pass `-nographics` to the editor, and revert the settings churn. Every sim PR that moves a golden also needs the WebGL `web_check`, and a re-recorded `smoke5` if the first five turns change. A PR that cannot run Unity says so, and it is not merged until someone with Unity has run it (CI does not run Unity). A route-ribbon re-bake (docs/routes.md, "Re-bake") is a Unity run too.
