-> **Owner decisions, 15 October 2026, on the sensitive rows** (given in the coordinator's session, recorded on #375: https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/issues/375#issuecomment-6183538544 and https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/issues/375#issuecomment-6183586870): Q-START-4, Q-CIV-1, Q-CIV-2, Q-CIV-3, Q-CIV-4 (its card total re-ruled later: https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/issues/375#issuecomment-6183762894), Q-ENEMY-5, Q-POW-1 to Q-POW-5, Q-ART-1 and Q-ART-3, each quoted in its row below. Q-HOLD-1, Q-HOLD-2 and Q-UI-2 were decided later the same day (https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/issues/375#issuecomment-6184081266). Q-ART-2 was decided on 17 October 2026. Where an answer sets no amount, the row says "value: open (owner)".
-
-These are **recommendations for the owner, not decisions.** Each one rests on the GDD, the impact plan, CONTENT_POLICY, the research (#419, #396, #570) or what the code does today, and prefers the smallest change. Two kinds of row carry no recommendation and say **"owner pick"**:
-- every question this plan marks sensitive: these list the options and one neutral line of context;
-- questions with no basis to ground a default.
-
-Where a row recommends a structure, its numbers enter `content/` as labelled design values in the PR that adds them, as Q-GEN-1 recommends. The owner sets or accepts them in that PR's review.
-
-**Two rows the Phase 2 answers may already decide.** #575 (Phase 2 PR 0) records the owner's "Take the recommendations" of 15 October 2026 as deciding D-G6 and D-C4 "as recommended".
-- **D-G6** reads "From events (sourced arms deals) and Money. Training and attacks consume it." That is the whole of Q-UNIT-3's supply question and Q-COMBAT-4's principle.
-- **D-C4** reads "The rung becomes derived (war state) and no longer sets turn length. The call-up is replaced by recruits once Phase 5 lands." That is Q-WAR-1's principle.
-
-**Decided (owner, 15 Oct 2026, "Take all recommendations"): both are treated as decided for Phase 5**, since the text matches. What stays open is only what the rows do not say: the amounts, what a shortfall does, and what derives the rung. Those parts are answered in the table below.
