-## Global constraints
-
-- The GDD wins over every older spec (AGENTS.md). Anything the GDD marks Open, Proposal or TBD is built only as the owner's answer. **No PR in this plan decides an open D-row.** Where this plan states a recommendation, it is a recommendation; the owner decides.
-- **Still open, and needed by this phase:** Q-MIN-2 under D-H3; Q-END-3 under D-H4; D-B5's N and texts (Q-DEF-2 and Q-DEF-4); Q-NEW-3; Q-OPEN-3 to Q-OPEN-5; D-B3 and D-B4's yishuvim part if Phase 4 has not settled them; and D-P and D-R before release. The questions below list each one. Every Phase 7 row with a recommended answer is decided on #784; the agents' drafts for the listed open questions still await the owner's approval.
-- **Sensitivity** (CONTENT_POLICY §2.3, §2.4 and §4; GDD owner ruling 1; impact plan §4):
-  - No option, effect, grant, score or end text rewards harm to civilians, from any side. The no-reward rule extends to the new effect kinds (R-EFX-005).
-  - The Holocaust is an event the player reacts to, never one the player plays, and it is shown without swastikas (§2.4). This binds the cutscene.
-  - No AI likeness of a real person in the cutscene (G3; CONTENT_POLICY §4).
-  - Every changed event card follows Q-CUT-4: a text or option change sends a `sensitivity-reviewed` card back to `fact-checked` until the owner re-reviews it.
-  - Rows of the question tables that touch war casualties, the Holocaust or civilians in the cutscene or the end texts carry **no recommendation**: they list options and neutral context, for the owner.
-  - Sensitivity tags and the release gates are left to the maintainer (AGENTS.md).
-- **Sourcing.** Every date, number and name in `content/` carries `sources:` with a `checked:` date. Event text uses office placeholders and no invented quotes (`docs/WRITING_EVENTS.md`). Dates show as "15 May 1948". Every image follows the event-image ruling ([docs/event-images.md](../../event-images.md); GPO, PD-Israel-only and CC BY-SA event photographs refused).
-- **Determinism** (docs/determinism.md): one RNG, no trigonometry, no unordered iteration into state, invariant culture. **No PR in this phase adds an RNG draw.** Structured effects apply in a fixed order (the option's list order, then ascending ids). Defeat counters are integers.
-- **Goldens.** Phase 7 runs after cutover, so each PR that changes an MVP rule or content re-pins every golden it moves, in the same PR, with a rebaseline-history row and the reason in the commit and the PR (spec §3, "After cutover"). Golden-moving PRs **merge one at a time**. New goldens: `scenario-mvp-defeat` (PR 5) and the full browser smoke `smoke-mvp` (PR 13).
-- **Rule IDs.** Every new rule gets an `R-` ID in `docs/rules/mvp.md`, defined in the code PR with its citing test. The IDs below are **proposed**. R-EFX continues Phase 2's R-EFX-001 and R-EFX-002 (Phase 5 named R-EFX-003 only "if Q-ARTY-3 builds D-H2 now", and Q-ARTY-3 did not, so Phase 7 defines it). R-GOV-003 was proposed in Phase 2 only if the defeat were built there; it was not, so it stays unused and Phase 7's defeat rules are R-END. New areas needing the maintainer's sign-off: **R-EVT** (event rules), **R-END** (the end and defeat), **R-SCORE** (the final score), **R-MIN** (ministers). R-OBJ continues after the last number Phases 3 and 4 take. Rewording a rule keeps its ID; a retired ID is not reused.
-- **Feature sections.** [docs/gdd/ministers-events-end.md](../../gdd/ministers-events-end.md) is the section for this phase. Update it (do not add a second one) as each PR lands; it must pass `gdd_lint.py`. #580 (draft) changes its end date to 15 January 1952 and states D-B5 as decided; rebase on it if it has merged.
-- **Each PR:** a branch from current `origin/main` in `.worktrees/<branch>`; a claimed issue (Task form); a `CHANGELOG.md` line for `sim/`, `content/` or `unity/`; the session's `Co-Authored-By` line on commits and its attribution line at the end of the PR body; "Refs #387" (only PR 13 may say "Fixes #387").
